# Keyswitch panel review for 382

Base: `eb55fa78dffe03356322e38dc59628f1508b9ae5` (main 0.3.381). Branch: `v2/w4-keyswitch-382`. Label fix: `a123ef22`; the following commit contains the list-detection guard and this report.

Two load-time metadata fixes use the existing articulation model:

- Areia showed sixteen note names instead of authored technique names. When a label is an autogenerated note name, every key in its range must agree on a nonempty authored name before that name replaces it. Meaningful existing labels and ambiguous ranges stay intact. This adapts v1 `0cb7a8a0:src/ui/panel.rs:758` and its named-key helper.
- Analog Strings invented 143 articulation rows from zero-sized auxiliary buttons and preset browser entries. Auto-detected choice lists now require positive height and switch-key evidence within that list. Keyless rows within a keyed list remain; existing recognized keyless articulations remain. Shape alone no longer creates articulation metadata.

For all 31 legitimate rows present in the baseline reports, source identities, key ranges, defaults, controls and switching ownership agree before/after. The focused label regression compares the entire instrument after restoring only labels. No overlay, input-routing, zone, or source-file edits are involved.

