## v1 and visual evidence

The frozen v1 hashes were verified. Its `ui` command completed for all ten NKI presets and records initialization UI metadata. Areia initializes with note labels starting at C-1; the saved preset's authored labels start at C-2. Initialization and saved-state values are separate evidence, so that difference is not classified as a range regression. The frozen `audit-ui --shots` binary lacks the shots feature; it was not rebuilt. v1 UVI and multi opener comparisons remain unknown.

Authored UI comparison uses loaded interface/keyboard metadata and v1 initialization metadata, not live Kontakt or UVI host windows. Empty recognized metadata is not proof that a native host has no dynamic switching controls.

Our corrected Areia captures at 1180×780 and 900×640 show the selected first row, matching performance header, trigger and red keyboard/stripe colours. Lower Areia rows need scrolling; their selected semantics still update. There is no automatic scroll-to-active change in this patch.

